WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.499
This is Continuum.

00:00:01.499 --> 00:00:06.844
Claude Code starts a task, Codex finishes it, and nothing is lost in between.

00:00:07.544 --> 00:00:10.935
First, connect both agents to your repository.

00:00:10.935 --> 00:00:12.188
One command each.

00:00:12.888 --> 00:00:18.461
Claude Code fixes the first bug, records the task and its next step, and stops.

00:00:19.161 --> 00:00:26.638
When Codex starts, Continuum briefs it automatically: what's done, what's left, and exactly what to do next.

00:00:27.338 --> 00:00:30.241
Codex picks up the same task and finishes it.

00:00:30.241 --> 00:00:34.629
Then you run the tests through Continuum, so the result is verified.

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:39.137
In the dashboard, it's one task, carried from one agent to the other.

00:00:39.837 --> 00:00:46.060
This check is verified: Continuum ran npm test against the exact contents of every file.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:51.032
Here are the acceptance criteria and steps, as the agents reported them.

00:00:51.732 --> 00:00:56.097
And here is the change itself, covered by the passing check.

00:00:56.797 --> 00:01:02.881
Every event is recorded in order: Claude Code's session, then Codex picking up the same task.

00:01:06.597 --> 00:01:08.123
Install it with one command.

00:01:08.123 --> 00:01:10.684
It runs on your machine, and nothing leaves it.
